        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 15: PowerShell 7 and the Raspberry Pi\nP\u00e1ginas: 386-407\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (386)\n\u2022 Introduction to the Raspberry Pi  (387)\n\u2022 Installing PowerShell 7 and VS Code  (388)\n  \u2022 Installing PowerShell  (388)\n  \u2022 Installing VS Code  (391)\n\u2022 Connecting remotely to the Pi  (391)\n  \u2022 Working with a headless Pi  (392)\n  \u2022 Connecting to the Pi with PowerShell  (395)\n  \u2022 Connecting to the Pi with VS Code  (397)\n\u2022 Running PowerShell on Raspberry Pi OS  (399)\n  \u2022 Installing the IoT module  (399)\n  \u2022 Exploring the IoT module  (400)\n\u2022 Simple physical computing  (402)\n\u2022 Summary  (406)\n\u2022 Questions  (406)\n\u2022 Further reading  (407)\n15\nPowerShell 7 and\nthe Raspberry Pi\nThis is one of the chapters I\u2019ve looked forward to writing the most. I\u2019ve got a house full of Raspberry\nPis (and Arduinos, micro:bits, and ESP32s\u2026). I use them to teach coding to school kids (and adults),\nas well as to run adblockers, media centers, wildlife cameras, and horticultural systems. I\u2019ve got one\nwith buttons that randomly selects episodes of my favorite radio shows and plays them (called the\nShendomizer). Mostly, I program them with Python, but PowerShell is also an option. We can even\ninstall a stripped-down version of Windows 10 on them, but we won\u2019t cover that in this book. Instead,\nwe\u2019ll look at how to install PowerShell 7 and Visual Studio ( VS ) Code, how to connect remotely to a\nheadless Pi over Wi-Fi using SSH with both PowerShell and VS Code, the default module for working\nwith PowerShell on the Raspberry Pi, and finish up by creating a script to accomplish the first steps\nin physical computing: getting an LED to blink on and off.\nThe main topics we\u2019ll cover in this chapter are as follows:\n\u2022I Introduction to the Raspberry Pi\n\u2022I Installing PowerShell and VS Code\n\u2022I Connecting remotely to the Pi\n\u2022I Running PowerShell on Raspberry Pi OS",
